  "finding": "Both pass the RL requirement (M-P1<50mm, max<d_max) with 0 emergencies and ~11 laps. In nominal the classical CV+PD baseline is slightly more accurate (RMSE 10.5 vs 14.2 mm, max 20.5 vs 56.7 mm) and far smoother (cage intervention 0.6-0.9% vs 82-86%: the RL CNN's jerky steering is continuously rate-limited by C-06). Nominal accuracy therefore does NOT favour the RL agent; its value must be demonstrated under perturbation/degradation where the CV estimator weakens \u2014 the robustness-world study."
